  "notes": "University Park. Major code 'MATSCI' avoids colliding with the MATSE department prefix. The capstone (MATSE 493W or 494W, a variable 0-3/1-3 credit split across two real terms per the bulletin) is simplified to one 3-credit item in a single term, matching how ME 441W-style capstone ambiguities have been resolved elsewhere. 'MATSE Specialization Course' (the Synthesis/Structure/Properties elective groups) and 'Technical Elective' pools are modeled generically, same convention as CMPSC's own open pools. Post-parens-fix re-scrape revealed CHEM 110's real prereq is MATH 22 (a placement threshold below Calc I that a MATH-140-track student has already tested past, but the bulletin's prereq text never says so explicitly), and MATH 22 has its own real chain (MATH 22 needs MATH 21, which needs MATH 4, which needs MATH 3) -- none of MATH 3/4/21/22 were in the plan, permanently blocking CHEM 110 and everything downstream of it (CHEM 111/113/202). Added MATH 3 (Semester 1), MATH 4 (Semester 2), MATH 21 (Semester 3), and MATH 22 (Semester 4) explicitly to complete the real chain, matching the fix used for MATH/MATHBA's identical STAT 200 gap. The added 12cr didn't fit in 8 terms at the original 17cr/semester cap (140.5cr total vs. 136cr capacity) -- raised max_credits_per_semester to 18, matching the cap already used by most other College of Engineering/Earth and Mineral Sciences majors in this dataset (AE, BME, CE, CHE, MINE, ME, NUCE, etc.), rather than silently letting the plan overflow into a 9th term.",
